      "message": "They will default to \"running\", right?\n\nJust want to make sure that console shows up by default when using servo without having to use any dut-control commands.\n\nThis was the default on my machine: \n\n  ~/trunk/src/scripts $ dut-control slp_s0\n  slp_s0:on\n\n  ~/trunk/src/scripts $ dut-control slp_s3\n  slp_s3:off\n\n\nwhich appeared to be the cause of unit test failures:\n   ./test/run_device_tests.py -t aes\n\n(More info on segger setup here: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/docs/fingerprint/fingerprint-debugging.md)\n\nWhen I turned both off, the unit test command worked:\n\n dut-control slp_s0:off\n\n\nWould be nice to add a sanity check unit test that reads the sleep signal GPIO just to make sure that they continue to be hooked up correctly (example of toggling dut-control: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/9263a4f135deb87f7926ed2e91deef496bbfe818/test/run_device_tests.py#169), but that would require disabling the sleep code when building for tests (TEST_BUILD) so it doesn\u0027t kill the console.",
